# MUT-PHANTOMGRANT2: the same phantom grant as MUT-PHANTOMGRANT, narrowed to fire only when the instruction
# request is low AND a fill is already in flight. That is the condition under which a surplus response can move
# a later assignment, because the cache pairs an incoming response to the oldest fill buffer expecting one by
# AGE with no address term. It is the shape that produced the arm-A measurement.
# The census lines are part of the mutation on purpose: they report how many idle cycles the run had and how
# many of those had any fill in flight, so a green result can be told apart from an absent injection.
# Applied to an out-of-tree archive only; the committed gen_agents_pkg.sv is never edited.
# Line ranges are against gen_agents_pkg.sv at 2e9b734 (blob fb3eb9f1716ee56b). Apply with:
#   git apply gen_mut_phantomgrant2.diff
# What it produces: the mutated file sha256 90a64e8767ba9ec0..., and build_sources_sha256 984932f3ed20d87f
# against d9a0553bd4e0b326 for the same tree without it.
--- a/dv/auto_dv/env/gen_agents_pkg.sv
+++ b/dv/auto_dv/env/gen_agents_pkg.sv
@@ -260,6 +260,7 @@
